{"id": "q0242", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "aggressive", "tier": "aggressive", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 580437262, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "c1188d4ab398808355719c420f025bd920b27aba798f5596eb328457a751cc63", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.5533501505851746, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 1, "query": "The lowest point on Earth is the bottom of the Mariana Trench at a depth of 35,840 feet below sea level. The highest point on Earth is the summit of Mt. Everest at a height of 29,028 feet above sea level. Which of the following is the best estimate of the distance between the lowest and highest points on Earth?\n\nA. 75,000 feet\nB. 65,000 feet\nC. 55,000 feet\nD. 60,000 feet\nE. 7,000 feet\nF. 64,000 feet\nG. 70,000 feet\nH. 50,000 feet\nI. 6,000 feet\nJ. 80,000 feet\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0242.wav", "input_sha256": "4e7d28604264753fb9e1a4de2796558a79cb54b5e50911b3dfb049871f86ce90", "input_samples": 677800, "input_s": 42.362, "n_real_chunks": 43, "score": 0.1422, "act": 0.9989, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "So let's figure out the total distance between the lowest and highest points. The Mariana Tren ch is 3 5 84 0 feet below sea level, and Mount Everest is 29, 280 feet above sea level. To get the total distance, we add those two numbers together. That gives us about 6 5,1 20 feet. Looking at the options, B is 65, 000 feet, which is very close to our calculation. So the best estimate is B.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 38, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 23, "feed_lag_max_ms": 541, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 1324,